<%# Upstream's own example: six boxes, one real input over them.

    Type into it and the boxes fill; the caret is drawn by the active box rather
    than by the input, whose own is transparent. Paste a six-digit code and it
    lands in one go, because the field the browser sees is an ordinary input.

    Labelled, and that is the caller's job here as it is upstream's: there is one
    input and it takes a name the way any input does. Unlabelled it fails axe,
    which is how this preview shipped for about an hour. %>
<div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
  <%= render(Shadcn::Label::Component.new(for: "otp-code")) { "Verification code" } %>
  <%= render(Shadcn::InputOtp::Component.new(max_length: 6, name: "code", input: { id: "otp-code" })) do %>
    <%= render(Shadcn::InputOtp::Group::Component.new) do %>
      <% 6.times do %>
        <%= render(Shadcn::InputOtp::Slot::Component.new) %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>
